        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/execute_requirement.py `_archive_delivered_task_state`: `local, remote = _git(integration, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").lower(), managed_task.target_main(integration)`. The error text reads 'local main {local} differs from origin main'. The `advance` caller does not appear to verify the branch inside this helper.",
                  "id": "archive-compares-head-not-main-branch",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The archive guard compares `git rev-parse HEAD` with origin/main, so it does not check that the checkout is on the main branch. A detached or feature-branch HEAD that happens to equal origin/main is treated as 'local main'. The refusal message also says 'local main' for what is really HEAD."
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
